course: dictionary
lesson: 9604
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word strike is a good example. «Lightning can strike the same place more than once.» Here strike means to hit something hard, because lightning does not ring or stop work.
explain: The same word can mean something different in a new sentence. «The clock will strike twelve at midnight.» Now strike means the clock rings to show the hour. Ask yourself: what is the sentence about? Then choose the meaning that fits.
explain: Some meanings belong to certain topics. «The bus drivers are on strike» means they have stopped working to ask for better pay. The words bus drivers and on strike are the clues. When you are unsure, read the words around it and try your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Strike can be a verb (to strike, struck) or a noun (a strike).
fact: To strike something means to hit it hard, as in «lightning struck the tree».
fact: A clock strikes when it rings to show the hour.
fact: To strike a match is to rub it to make a flame.
fact: A strike is when workers stop working to ask for better pay or conditions.
exercise: «Lightning can strike the same place more than once.» What does strike mean here? | To stop work to ask for more pay | *To hit something hard | To ring to show the hour | To rub something to make a flame
exercise: «The clock will strike twelve at midnight.» What does strike mean here? | To stop working for pay | *To ring to show the hour | To make a flame | To hit something hard
exercise: «The bus drivers are on strike, so the buses have stopped.» What is a strike? | *Workers stopping work to ask for better pay or conditions | A ringing clock | To make a flame | Hitting something hard
test: «Strike a match carefully, because the flame is hot.» What does strike a match mean? | To hit the match hard so it breaks | To blow the match out | *To rub it to make a flame | To count the matches
test: «An idea struck her while she was in the bath.» What does struck mean here? | Hit her hard | Stopped working to ask for pay | *Suddenly came into her mind | Rang loudly to show the time
exam: «When Mia rolled the ball, it knocked all ten pins down, so she got a strike.» What does strike mean in bowling? | Ringing to show the hour | Hit hard | Rubbing to make a flame | *Knocking all the pins down
